xt","text":"20√n."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on M, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the complement of their vectors checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"largest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and nonnegative, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale. The dense solver throws as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacencySpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/laplacianEigenpairs(largest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-1nz26","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","t